IN THE HIGH COURT OF DELHI
CASE NO: CS(COMM) 1601 of 2016
CITATION: 2016 SCC OnLine Del 6229
YEAR: 2016

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Pradeep Nandrajog, Yogesh Khanna

PARTIES:
Oxford University Press vs Rameshwari Photocopy

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Copyright Act, 1957

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 52(1)(i) Copyright Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
fair use in education, course packs, educational exception, copyright infringement

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that creation of course packs by photocopiers for students is protected under Section 52(1)(i) of the Copyright Act as fair use for educational instruction.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 52(1)(i) Copyright Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

